<% content_for :sidebar do %>
  <div class="sidebar-stack">
    <%= link_to "Back Home", "/achievements/", class: "sidebar-button" %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<section class="chain-index help-page">
  <header class="chain-index__header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Help</p>
    <h1>About Achievement Chains</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="chain-card">
    <p>
      One day I stepped out of the shower and I realised that I had this idea to make a project called "Achievement Chains", so here it is.
    </p>
    <p>
      The idea is that everyone can make their own chains and share with others. Then others can favorite/follow/add to their library and track their progress. Or just for yourself, if you want to plan your achievement journey and track it in a more visual way.
    </p>
    <p>
      Why chains? There are many strategic (and not so strategic) games with hundreds of achievements, but there isn't always a clear way to know how to get to a certain achievement, or what milestones you'll certainly have too meet before reaching your final goal. This tool is meant to help with that by suggesting a path to the goals you choose, and letting you track your progress along that path.
    </p>
    <p>
      On another day when I already had a big part of this project done, I wrote about it:
    </p>
    <p>
      I want to build something about making achievements into meaningful journeys for someone who doesn't know where to start with a game. Or did the main story and doesn't know what to do next.
    </p>
    <p>
      What else planned? Community Goals - like regular achievements but without its steam counterpart, to better navigate player along their journey.
    </p>
    <p>
      Is this an open-source project? Not at the moment, but I've been considering open-sourcing it after the initial launch if it gets traction and if there is interest in the community to contribute.
    </p>
    <p>
      And who am I? I'm just someone who likes steam achievements... For questions and suggestions you can find me <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199079570785/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
